WHY PROPRIETARY, AND WHY NOW (recorded 2026-08-14, founder decision W11-04)

RepoPulse is not going public until a clean self-hosted install is proven
working end to end. This license states that position rather than leaving it
implied by the absence of a file.

The choice is deliberately the REVERSIBLE one. Proprietary today can become any
open-source license later; an open-source grant, once published, cannot be
withdrawn from the copies it created. Choosing an OSS license before the product
is distributable would be making an irreversible decision to save writing one
file.

This is a business decision recorded by its author, not legal advice. Have a
lawyer review before the first actual distribution, whichever direction it goes.
